Z||000004||Chris Schaefer||04-01-2001||09:37 PM||||Hey Larry,<P>As always you took great photo's.  I would like to use them and get a story from you for the FOCONE 3rd quarter magazine.  Let me know.<P>Lisa,<P>I just looked at your photo's also.  I see that you took a picture of a 3.4L DOHC V6 that is in a silver/purple GT.  You have is saved as a V8motor.  Just thought you would like to know.  BTW, your photo's are also top-notch.<P>I wish I could have been there.  You know, sun, sand and warmth.||||reg||10
Z||000005||mrfixit58||04-02-2001||07:41 AM||||Hey Lar,<P>Nice pics. I need to print the picture of the Chief Judge -- who is also the president of Suncoast Fieros. Lovely profile! I noticed the picture of your car. Were you in the "Stock" or "Street Stock" class? Did you place?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||Old Lar||04-02-2001||08:28 AM||||I was in stock, a tough class this year as all stock GT fastbacks were grouped together (86,87 and 88).  Tough to win with a 1700 mile GT in the running as well as other low milage cars.  I didn't place.  I didn't even get a door prize.<P>I still have more pictures coming.  I resized these photos to ~4x6 so they would download in a short time.  My digital camera stores them at 24x16..2.1 million pixel resolution.<P>Lisa, you take a great photo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Cheever2||04-02-2001||08:41 AM||||Good pics from both of you.  Thanks.<P>Lar, what's the story on that convertible with the extended nose?  Did it look better in person?  Looks kinda silly to me.<BR>||||reg||6
